sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor U as User
  participant B as Browser
  participant H as user.Notifications<br/>(notification.go) ✎
  participant M as activities model ✎
  participant DB as Database

  U->>B: clicks "Group by repository"
  B->>H: GET /notifications?group=repo
  rect rgb(219, 231, 251)
    H->>H: parseNotificationFilter(ctx) ✎ gives GroupByRepo = true
    Note right of H: Decision 3: group=repo is kept in the URL
  end
  rect rgb(217, 242, 223)
    H->>M: db.Find[Notification](opts with GroupByRepo) ★
    M->>DB: SELECT ... JOIN repository ORDER BY LOWER(owner_name),<br/>lower_name, updated_unix DESC, id DESC
    Note over M,DB: Decisions 1 and 2: SQL keeps each repository's rows<br/>together, with repositories sorted A-Z
    DB-->>M: one page of notifications
    M-->>H: notifications
    H->>M: CountNotificationsByRepo(unread opts) ★
    M->>DB: SELECT repo_id, COUNT(*) ... GROUP BY repo_id
    DB-->>M: unread count per repository
    M-->>H: map[repoID]count
  end
  H->>M: LoadRepos(), LoadIssues(), LoadComments()
  M-->>H: notifications with repository and issue loaded
  rect rgb(217, 242, 223)
    H->>H: groupNotificationsByRepo(...) ★
    Note right of H: new section each time RepoID changes
  end
  H-->>B: HTML with one section per repository
  rect rgb(217, 242, 223)
    B->>B: initNotificationGroups() ★ restores collapsed sections
  end
